# CMS package (`@repo/cms`)

Portable Sanity data layer — schemas, queries, client, and live preview. No Studio UI or plugins here.

## Exports

| Subpath | Module |
|---------|--------|
| `@repo/cms` | index |
| `@repo/cms/client` | Sanity client |
| `@repo/cms/env` | `isSanityConfigured()` |
| `@repo/cms/live` | `sanityFetch`, `SanityLive` |
| `@repo/cms/queries` | GROQ queries |
| `@repo/cms/schemas` | Schema definitions |

## Schema conventions

- Use `defineType` + `defineField` from `sanity`.
- File names: kebab-case (`site-settings.ts`). Export names: camelCase (`siteSettings`).
- Add `validation: (Rule) => Rule.required()` on title and slug fields.
- Include `preview` config and `orderings` on listable documents.
- Register new types in `src/schemas/index.ts`.

## GROQ queries

Always use `defineQuery` from `next-sanity` for typegen compatibility:

```ts
export const projectQuery = defineQuery(`
  *[_type == "project" && slug.current == $slug][0] { ... }
`)
```

When adding or changing a query field list, update the corresponding schema if needed.

## Typegen (required for schema changes)

```bash
pnpm cms:typegen
```

Config: `packages/cms/sanity-typegen.json` → generates `src/sanity.types.ts`.

After schema changes:
1. Run typegen.
2. Commit `schema.json` and `sanity.types.ts` together with schema edits.
3. Prefer generated types over manual casts from `types.ts`.

## Env

`isSanityConfigured()` checks `projectId` and `dataset`. Never hardcode Sanity project IDs in source.

## Images

Use `@sanity/image-url` helpers when building image URLs. Featured images should have alt text validation where applicable.
